{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1419123-why-don-t-scions-conquer-the-world","id":1419123,"title":"Why don't scions conquer the world?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-10-19T21:56:06-07:00","id":1419123,"title":"Why don't scions conquer the world?","content":"So with all of the skills at the scion's disposal, why don't we see scions regularly sitting in positions of power and prestige? I doubt any normal mortal could defeat the appropriate scion for the presidency or stop a child of ares added to a special forces team. I am only part way through scion origins now so I may be missing something. Instead I am thinking of doing a campaign where the premise would be broad world wide geopolitics in the face of an apocalypse. What barriers prevent scions from just becoming an elite ruling class in the world?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-19T22:07:28-07:00","id":1419124,"title":"","content":"Generally speaking, not much stops them, it\u2019s just usually most Scions have enough on their plate without adding being the ruler of a nation on top of it, that and also ruling a nation is not as fun as it sounds most Scions probably enjoy adventuring and forging their Legend too much to become a normal ruler other then coming in to make some divine pronouncements every so often.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-19T23:29:34-07:00","id":1419130,"title":"","content":"So this is a bit of a weird topic and there's several ways to approach this. To begin with the very meta answer is quite simply that the reason scions don't have positions of power like that is because it would mess with the base concept of The World which is suposed to resemble ours but magical. If you absolutely need in universe answers here are a couple. <br /> <br /> 1. It's just a political mess on a divine level. Imagine if Joe scion of Poseidon declares himself god king of Canada. How do you think the first nations pantheon would feel? What about other theoi that just don't want him or think they should be in charge? Distant support for at least vaguely secular leadership is simply less hassle for the gods at large. <br /> <br /> 2. Many mortals don't want it. Sure a group of hero tier scions could feasibly take over a nation. It's very not outside the field of possibility. And it might even seem great for a moment until fate decides they need a test.. and another one.. and another.. and then the scions in charge have a episode where they realize what they have simply isn't enough and must conquer more. If your a mortal it's not unreasonable to not want that stuff and do everything in your power to stop it. Scions aren't invincible afterall.<br /> <br /> 3. Why would a scion want to when there are far easier ways to obtain power and prestige if they seek it. Money can just be taken, land can be claimed in any weird terra incognita, influence can be asserted all over the world through building a big business and fame is right at the push of a button on the net. What can ruling a nation give that any but the most powerhungry people want? <br /> <br /> That said if you want to play in a world where scions openly take positions of power by force or modern politics it isnt totally unreasonable and in some ways It's actually closer to the myths the game is based on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26499-bluishpurple","name":"bluishpurple","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-19T23:31:48-07:00","id":1419131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RadioFreeDeath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1419123-why-don-t-scions-conquer-the-world#post1419123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So with all of the skills at the scion's disposal, why don't we see scions regularly sitting in positions of power and prestige? I doubt any normal mortal could defeat the appropriate scion for the presidency or stop a child of ares added to a special forces team. I am only part way through scion origins now so I may be missing something. Instead I am thinking of doing a campaign where the premise would be broad world wide geopolitics in the face of an apocalypse. What barriers prevent scions from just becoming an elite ruling class in the world?</div> </div> </div> </div>Historically they obviously did based on who the great kings and conquerors of myth are. Clearly something changed to keep Scions out of political power - the divine motive for Order gods toward that end is pretty clear: Fate assures Scion reigns are epics. That is quite a bit counter to any goal toward stability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 10-20-2020, 04:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-20T00:25:07-07:00","id":1419132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1419123-why-don-t-scions-conquer-the-world?p=1419131#post1419131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Historically they obviously did based on who the great kings and conquered of myth are. Clearly something changed to keep Scions out of political power - the divine motive for Order gods toward that end is pretty clear: Fate assures Scion reigns are epics. That quite a bit counter to any goal toward stability.</div> </div> </div> </div>For one particularly poignant example, remember Alexander the Great? The conqueror who wanted to Hellenize the entire world, and got pretty far in doing so? The moment he died, and I do mean that very <i>moment</i>, it <b><i>all</i></b> fell into ruin and infighting. Sure, your Scions may be very charismatic and persuasive, even virtuous and exemplary, but... once they're gone, will they have anything left that can remotely be considered a physical legacy, rather than just an oratory one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-20T02:05:17-07:00","id":1419137,"title":"","content":"Scions are members of a bigger society, being king of a country is not more than being the class representative during high school, it is a big deal, but yet it\u2019s almost irrelevant to the adults, in this case the gods.<br /> <br /> Also, heroes burn bright and for short. Their powers come from doing legendary things, not mundane. Being the creator of a culture is legendary, founding the capital city is legendary, being the first emperor is legendary, being the 44th president is kind of mundane (a big deal, but yet mundane). Alexander, Julius Caesar, and other semi-legendary names in history, did great things, most died in the climax of their stories, or just stoped doing legendary stuff and died mere mortals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-20T05:42:40-07:00","id":1419150,"title":"","content":"While a lot of scions stay at the Hero level for their whole lives, a fair number are striving to become Demigods. There is no way a Demigod could conquer the world and still have the time and energy to actually advance toward apotheosis. Also, they'll be more fatebinding problems for a Demigod than a Hero.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-20T09:06:00-07:00","id":1419175,"title":"","content":"What's to say they <i>don't </i>actually do this? In my games it is primarily the Origin level characters who go for mundane power, influence and prestige because they are still mostly human with human wants and desires. When they get to Hero they may still do this but by then the political power is mostly just as a means to a bigger end for them. I don't plan on running Demigod but if I did then the earthly political game would be way past its relevance for the characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-20T12:34:33-07:00","id":1419201,"title":"","content":"Remember Iulius Caesar? He tried. In Scion Lore, he's a god, Iulius Divine. His conquest campaigns were building his legend, and he was favored by Venus.<br /> <br /> As for why there's no major stratification for Scions on Top as the Ruling Class... Me personally? I don't think there's enough Scions for that to be sustainable. If you build a nation around yourself and your blessings but leave it without some kind of succession plan, you can't be sure it will maintain its previous glory without you.<br /> <br /> And well, there's a section in Origin that I love. Something to the effect of:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> About as many leaders in the World claim divine favor as they do in our world. Some of them may even be right. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-20T13:18:08-07:00","id":1419209,"title":"","content":"These all seem like good barriers I could actually build into a scion campaign premise I think. Im thinking a set of scions who realize they have to prepare for a serious threat of some sort. So they conquer a nation either through election or force. But then they are faced with other pantheons who dont want to be under their thumb. Secret mortal societies who have worked for centuries to keep scions out of power because of their instability. Multitasking their apotheosis. I think it's shaping up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-20T13:20:08-07:00","id":1419210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1419123-why-don-t-scions-conquer-the-world?p=1419201#post1419201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember Iulius Caesar? He tried. In Scion Lore, he's a god, Iulius Divine. His conquest campaigns were building his legend, and he was favored by Venus.<br /> <br /> As for why there's no major stratification for Scions on Top as the Ruling Class... Me personally? I don't think there's enough Scions for that to be sustainable. If you build a nation around yourself and your blessings but leave it without some kind of succession plan, you can't be sure it will maintain its previous glory without you.<br /> <br /> And well, there's a section in Origin that I love. Something to the effect of:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's just notable in myth that Scions claiming crowns is almost the default in epic myths, but it'd be an outlier for Scions in the modern World, so something presumably has shifted since the origin eras of the myths. My take is that the attitude of the gods themselves have shifted on the topic, and while their are exceptions among the gods, as well as Scions willing to defy the gods on the topic, it's enough to set a norm that those cases are defying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-20T13:22:40-07:00","id":1419214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1419123-why-don-t-scions-conquer-the-world?p=1419210#post1419210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It's just notable in myth that Scions claiming crowns is almost the default in epic myths, but it'd be an outlier for Scions in the modern World, so something presumably has shifted since the origin eras of the myths. My take is that the attitude of the gods themselves have shifted on the topic, and while their are exceptions among the gods, as well as Scions willing to defy the gods on the topic, it's enough to set a norm that those cases are defying.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's working out exactly what that shift In perceptions is. Imagine I need to stop gorgumond. I imagine having the might of the us military at my disposal would be useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-20T13:42:08-07:00","id":1419219,"title":"","content":"I also have to question. Are most nobility in myth really scions? For every demigod king I can actually think of a shitton more who at best have some distant divine relationships in the backgrounds. Oftentimes heroes serve under mortal kings","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26499-bluishpurple","name":"bluishpurple","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-20T13:46:12-07:00","id":1419220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bluishpurple</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1419123-why-don-t-scions-conquer-the-world?p=1419219#post1419219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also have to question. Are most nobility in myth really scions? For every demigod king I can actually think of a shitton more who at best have some distant divine relationships in the backgrounds. Oftentimes heroes serve under mortal kings</div> </div> </div> </div>They tend to be either demigods or at least the descendants of demigods. Take Menelaus, for example: not personally a demigod, but part of a VERY prestigious divine lineage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-20T14:27:49-07:00","id":1419233,"title":"","content":"This is all true. <br /> <br /> What you're likely to run into:<br /> <br /> 1.) Seeking political power is hard to do on the side. It requires a lot of focus, for reasons we're about to come to:<br /> <br /> 2.) Scions are rare. Denizens are less so. Worshippers abound. You are likely to run afoul of those as you ascend to the throne, or to office. Depending on how it goes, any of those may get Gods involved, and while Aphrodite or Lugh aren't going to appear and smack you in the face with the whole of their divine might, if you haven't sufficiently appeased them yourself then you're setting yourself up for a bad time.<br /> <br /> 3.) Speaking of other scions, you aren't the first or the last to pursue temporal power with divine backing. Hell, Fate being the lover of cheap drama it is, it's actual tremendously likely you'll encounter another Scion seeking the same powers and respect you are.<br /> <br /> Aaaand that brings a whole new level of politics into play: if you're opposed by another Scion, then we get into the relationship between your respective gods. If they're friendly, does your god want you to go easier on them? If they're nemeses, is this about to get more vicious than you can stomach? Is this about to be a wager you don't care to be a part of?<br /> <br /> 4.) Assuming competence and heroic action, your conquest will grow, but the duties of administration will grow faster. Of those who pursue dominion and conquest of people and lands, only a fraction find any pleasure in their maintenance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-20T16:31:53-07:00","id":1419258,"title":"","content":"Though I don't think &quot;Running the state is something to do on the side while you work on your Legend&quot; is the right way to think about it.<br /> <br /> If raising and running a city-state using your Creator and Leader Callings isn't building your Legend through methods other than punching face <i>I don't know what is</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 10-20-2020, 07:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-20T17:05:43-07:00","id":1419262,"title":"","content":"If you've got a copy of Mysteries of the World, I suppose the answer depends on where you've got your Dials set, doesn't it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>She/Her pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12975-zealot_vedas","name":"Zealot_Vedas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12975_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-20T17:15:51-07:00","id":1419266,"title":"","content":"Who says they don't...?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-20T21:46:34-07:00","id":1419295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1419123-why-don-t-scions-conquer-the-world?p=1419266#post1419266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who says they don't...?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well as Divis Iulius and Divis Augustus proved, I don\u2019t think the illusion of republicanism is sustainable with Scions claiming and exercising divine right to rule. So if the United States with all the associated recognizable cultural touchstones exist in the setting, something must have checked the rise of an absolute divine ruler for the past 244 years - and same for all other electoral republics and parliamentary democracies as well.<br /> <br /> edit: then again I suppose there is a broader problem here with why would it even occur to anyone make as self-evidently false a claim as \u201call men are created equal\u201d in a World where Scions exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 10-21-2020, 12:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-21T00:08:16-07:00","id":1419317,"title":"","content":"I think this is one of those things that really shines a light on the weaknesses of &quot;The world of Scion is the same as our world, but with more Gods&quot; - I have never felt that the world could possibly be the same if all of the old faiths continued to exist as powerful and distinct organizations/cults/gatherings across the globe. And the presence of Scions throughout all those millennia would absolutely have a direct impact on how history went, and how it will go in the future.<br /> <br /> For all of the failings of Scion 1st Edition, the plot device of &quot;once the Titans were defeated, the Gods became semi-retired, and life went on; now the Titans are awake again, and Gods and Scions will return to the World&quot; made it a lot easier to start with &quot;our world&quot;, and go off from there.<br /> <br /> But unless you are going to write an alternate history supplement that fits the official game world [and it's pretty obvious that <i>no-one</i> would agree on exactly how to do that], it's up to every ST to figure it out for themselves. And if you want Scions to alter the world in your campaign, you can and should go right ahead and do that,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-21T06:59:39-07:00","id":1419369,"title":"","content":"I think the simplist reason is just Scions did continue to be in places of power, they just didn\u2019t have much of a global effect, cause most Scions are Heroes and Origin tier who are primarily regional in their reach, only a very tiny minority ever become Demigods who have a much larger reach and effect","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-21T07:24:17-07:00","id":1419373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1419123-why-don-t-scions-conquer-the-world?p=1419317#post1419317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this is one of those things that really shines a light on the weaknesses of &quot;The world of Scion is the same as our world, but with more Gods&quot; - I have never felt that the world could possibly be the same if all of the old faiths continued to exist as powerful and distinct organizations/cults/gatherings across the globe. And the presence of Scions throughout all those millennia would absolutely have a direct impact on how history went, and how it will go in the future.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can apply that to literally any other work of fiction that goes &quot;Like Our World But-&quot;. World of Darkness? &quot;Oh you expect me to believe that these vampires and werewolves and stuff had some history book from the future and so knew exactly when to and when not to interfere, so this world turned out much the same as all the others? Yeah right, pull the other one.&quot;<br /> <br /> Superheroes? &quot;P-SHAW, even if we assume that Metahumans only started showing up in high numbers a bit after World War II, the entire world map should be redrawn because they would have shaped literally every other facet&quot;<br /> <br /> But the responses to those is &quot;Look if we don't assume some level of similarity to how OUR world turned out, then it won't feel familiar and lose the appeal of playing a game that is in something much like our world.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's a little suspension of disbelief that's really not a huge ask compared to most other forms of fiction but I don't see a lot of people getting bent out of shape about how, say, vampire cartels should have changed the entire shape of history in Vampire.<br /> <br /> Not to mention that it REALLY hits me the wrong way to tell the faithful (Reminder that <b>basically every Pantheon in the Hero and Companion books are still actively worshipped</b> with the exception of the Teros because they're entirely fictional) &quot;So uh, realtalk: If your Gods existed the world would look entirely different. It's a lie, they're ignoring you or fake. I am very smart&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 10-21-2020, 10:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-21T09:14:00-07:00","id":1419383,"title":"","content":"Wait Obama wasn't a Scion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-21T12:31:38-07:00","id":1419412,"title":"","content":"The superhero thing bothers me as well, and I make changes in any campaign I run to reflect them influencing history. Ditto any Scion-style campaign I run. YMMV. <br /> As for the other faiths - I didn't say other religions don't exist, aren't valid, or any such thing. However, I think it's fair to say that worship of (for example) the Theoi is very different than it once was. And there are few stories of the sort of &quot;giant monster/demon/dragon threatens city, Scion saves the day with magical weapon&quot; sort these days. The game (which is what I'm talking about here) is based on a larger-than-life premise that, for my money at least, begs historical changes. However, you can play it any way you like - I was just stating what my thoughts were, that's all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-21T13:31:42-07:00","id":1419421,"title":"","content":"Sorry I got snippy, just... I see a LOT of what seem like bad-faith (pun not intended) takes with people critiquing the setting and most of them basically boil down to the comments I made, and a nonzero number of them give the likes of Masquerade Urban Fantasy settings (especially World of Darkness) a pass because, to be frank, they're used to just shrugging and going &quot;Yeah sure&quot; at something that's really not a better handwave than &quot;The World looks like ours in places Just Because&quot;<br /> <br /> Because like... In WoD, the Vampire Clans don't have a history book from the future to let them know whether or not to kill this stumbling drunk in 1932 because turns out this person is actually going to found a business in six years. Going &quot;This World has always had monsters and predators but they pretend not to do anything and history just so happened to align&quot; is, if you think about it, as big an ask as &quot;The Gods are real, Heroes exist, people know this, many of the Faiths have continued to this day, also the World looks a lot like our World&quot;<br /> <br /> Just that, y'know, the entire Urban Fantasy genre has made the idea of a Masquerade so ubiquitous that most fans don't bother asking.<br /> <br /> Now if &quot;The history happens to align closely enough&quot; makes your brainspiders creep up (which I have full sympathy for, having a few brainspiders of my own) then a take you can go with is &quot;The Gods were always worshipped, but they, for reasons known only to them, mostly kept things backstage. They maintained the World, they blessed discretely, but their Champions became fewer in number. Until now. Now is the dawn of a new Heroic age.&quot;<br /> <br /> I don't buy into the whole 'Oh noes the Second Titanomachy is making them more active&quot; because like... Whaddya mean 'SECOND' Titanomachy? Ask the Netjer, the Teotl, or the Deva if their Titans were sealed away. They kind of demonstrably are not. What makes THIS year of nightly battles against their ancient enemy different than... All the previous ones? Their Titans were never gone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 10-21-2020, 04:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-21T14:51:03-07:00","id":1419448,"title":"","content":"I do like the idea of a new Age of Heroes","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-21T15:51:14-07:00","id":1419467,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the WoD Masquerade didn't do it for me, either - I'm the guy who wonders why Sam and Dean aren't in jail by now. Everyone can do what works, that's cool. But I would either a) do what I did, and start waking Gods/Scions (and changing history) from a certain point on (such as 2000, 2012, 2050, or whatever), or else b) rewrite the last 2,000 years of history to tell whatever story I want to tell, and hopefully have players who will enjoy the speculative fiction. That's just what works for me and my brain spiders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-21T16:17:42-07:00","id":1419473,"title":"","content":"What i do is although the gods are always as present as they feel like being, the presence and numbers of scions on the other hand tend to ebb and flow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-21T18:30:40-07:00","id":1419494,"title":"","content":"The most basic answer to &quot;why don't Scions conquer the world?&quot; is that other Scions - rivals, enemies, or just anyone with a different agenda or ideal of what the World should be like - are going to oppose their efforts. <br /> <br /> (This also holds true for superhero/superhuman settings - Trinity Continuum's Aberrant, for example - as well. DC's Kingdom Come - and it's inferior copy of the Injustice: Gods Among Us game - and Marvel's Squadron Supreme miniseries are both built on this idea. Watchmen deals with it to a degree as well.)<br /> <br /> It's also entirely possibly that certain activities may play too heavily into one of your Pantheon's Virtues. Egotism and hubris may run rampant for one of the Theoi, while Teotl may find themselves willing to Sacrifice far too much. On the other hand, a Kami (or Devi) may decide that both Sincerity and Right Action (or Conscience and Duty) dictate that she become Japan's (or India's) new Prime Minister or one of the Aesir may decide that Audacity pretty much demands that he try to conquer the world (especially if he believes its his Wyrd/fate). <br /> <br /> As far as the issue of the World looking like our world - or not - I will recommend the idea of looking at the Wild Talents (a superhero RPG) <a href=\"https://www.rpglibrary.org/utils/wild_talents_axes/\" target=\"_blank\">Axes of Design</a>. These are very similar to the Dials from Mysteries of the World, and deal with the areas of Historical Inertia, Talent (or in our case Scion) Inertia, Moral Clarity, and The Beautiful &amp; The Pointless. <br /> <br /> In the case of Historical Inertia, you'd have the same Iron, Heroic, Bronze, Silver and Gold levels as our Scion Dials, just inverted from how the Wild Talents Axes are. With Iron Historical Inertia, [paraphrasing from the Axes] Scions don't change the course of history, but can make it my stopping Titanic monsters and threats, preventing other Scions from causing damage, and the like. But even if a rampaging dragon destroys downtown Chicago, it gets rebuilt in a year or so. With Gold Historical Inertia, Scions change the course of history all the time, and may the best Scion win. A Scion helped Cornwallis defeat the American Rebellion. A band of Scions founded the first Mars colony in the 1950s. Probably every important thing ever invented or carried out was centered around a Scion. Those are just the two extremes. I suspect most games are probably going to default to a Bronze or Silver level of Historical Inertia. And if you go with the idea that The World largely looks like our world, at least until very recently, then it's entirely possible that for whatever reason the World was probably at Heroic or Bronze Historical Inertia before moving up to its current Bronze or Silver level (which just so happens to coincide with the PCs becoming active Heroes). <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-21T22:20:09-07:00","id":1419515,"title":"","content":"I personally find the &quot;declare random historical figures are really supernatural beings&quot; in a supernatural world far more interesting than the hands off approach. SO yeah there's been plenty of Scion presidents, kings.. what have you. And plenty of mundane kings. History is long. If you want to play a game about becoming Godking of Canada. That is the game you play. Why isn't the current prime minister a godking? IS that really any different than &quot;why hasn't someone already killed this dragon&quot;? Why are there any monsters left if there were scions in the past?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-22T09:30:16-07:00","id":1419596,"title":"","content":"I like to go with the option that Scions could potentially lead an army or rule over a state but they are just a small pawn within the divine politics that governs the world. Fate may decide which direction a Scion should go in to live their lives. Some mortals may have divine backing to do so. No matter how a Scion tries, they probably won't get to be the President of the Dominican Republic because Eshu and Oshun love the candidates running for office. Whatever Social rolls the Scion pulls, the gods won't let them have this one. As long as gods like Tezcatlipoca, Loki, or Macha exist, their representation of entropy sort of ensures that these Scions are still subject to the divine will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Pantheon(s):<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1LMQFZLq3NrOHs2cp7OWnfukuHCNI4h_0/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Nat, the Spirits of Myanmar</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1WDvOmQCR3a25WbVowfe8KgGbGLU0yzX3/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Phi, the Spirits of the Tai People</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13670-svarogg","name":"Svarogg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13670_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-22T10:29:29-07:00","id":1419604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Svarogg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1419123-why-don-t-scions-conquer-the-world?p=1419596#post1419596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No matter how a Scion tries, they probably won't get to be the President of the Dominican Republic because Eshu and Oshun love the candidates running for office.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, if your game needs a Hero (PC or NPC) to become President of the Dominican republic, that can happen. Like, Neall himself said that it's entirely possible that some places DO have Scion heads of state, and I noted that you could make &quot;Become Prime Minister of a country&quot; as part of building your legend.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-22T22:29:17-07:00","id":1419719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1419123-why-don-t-scions-conquer-the-world?p=1419604#post1419604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, if your game needs a Hero (PC or NPC) to become President of the Dominican republic, that can happen. Like, Neall himself said that it's entirely possible that some places DO have Scion heads of state, and I noted that you could make &quot;Become Prime Minister of a country&quot; as part of building your legend.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh no confusion intended. I was trying to rationalize the question that OP posed, &quot;what barriers prevent Scions from just becoming an elite ruling class in the world.&quot; It's totally workable for a player to try and become a head of state or have divine mandate on your side.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Pantheon(s):<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1LMQFZLq3NrOHs2cp7OWnfukuHCNI4h_0/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Nat, the Spirits of Myanmar</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1WDvOmQCR3a25WbVowfe8KgGbGLU0yzX3/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Phi, the Spirits of the Tai People</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13670-svarogg","name":"Svarogg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13670_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-23T10:47:45-07:00","id":1419811,"title":"","content":"There basically are no barriers, to be frank, beyond &quot;The GM doesn't want to deal with that&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-24T13:03:00-07:00","id":1420010,"title":"","content":"My general approach is, a lot of them did. Alexander the Great, Julius Caesar, Genghis Khan, the Pharaohs of Egypt, the still-reigning Emperor of Japan. A whole lot of Scions are responsible for many of the founding bloodlines and/or empires that left remarkable impacts upon the history of the world. Many of the pantheons in the World have little to no differentiation between religious and secular power structures and actively encouraged scions ruling over parts of the World. Granted many of the more ambitious scions tend to die suitably dramatic deaths before they ever manage total world conquest. (Likely Fate considers an eternal God King ruling over all of the world to be disagreeable)<br /> <br /> Now in modern history this has become less common. Democracy and Republican nation-states are less-conducive to long bloodlines dominating the country, and things have changed for God-kings. I'd say a lot of this is because Scions weren't quite as common for much of the modern era and in that interim some public opinion shifted. It's also possible that a number of pantheons changed their minds on monarchy (possibly noticing that even if the Scion who founded the dynasty was a proper heroic type, there was no guarantee that the next king was going to be any good. (Which is kind of the problem with monarchies in general)).<br /> <br /> Personally I'd say that in the History of the World, one of the last big Scion kings in the Western world was probably Louis XIV, Scion of Apollo and the so-called Sun King. He was pretty much the epitome of the model of kingship for the Theoi, practically a Roman Emperor, reigned for over 70 years, and was basically the centerpiece of absolute power in Europe. (&quot;I am the State&quot; and all that.)<br /> <br /> And then two kings later down the dynasty and the general populace was ready to cut all the nobles' heads off. Napoleon might have been a Scion as well, but Europe shut him down hard once they took him down.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile across the sea, a few Scions, most prominently a fellow named George Washington, decide to make a Republic symbolically modelled after the Roman Republic and the Greek Democratic City states. Washington gets so much legend from the revolution that he actually achieves a form of Apotheosis (they even make a fresco of the event in the Capitol building after the fact, literally titled &quot;The Apotheosis of Washington&quot;), but rather specifically refuses kingship in establishing the Presidency. They build a capital directly inspired by classical Greco-Roman and Egyptian monuments, and construct a whole civic mythology around the lives of their founding fathers.<br /> <br /> The whole thing is very deliberately an attempt to form a Republican system that the Gods will approve of, and it succeeds. (In my version of the World, American currency reads &quot;One Nation Under the Gods&quot;) Republican systems gain authority over monarchies in Europe over time. Scions still show up in these political systems, but not in large numbers, and the Republican system has enough tacit approval that the Gods generally discourage deliberate autocratic power grabs. Whether that trend will continue now that scions are becoming more common and *insert campaign events here* starts shaking things up, will depend a lot on how these new Scions behave.<br /> <br /> (I will also note that this is very distinctly a Western, and admittedly an Amero-centric look at these events. Go outside the states and mythological historians are likely to point out a dozen other events that led to the shifting of Divine opinion on supporting Republican nation states rather than giving all the credit to the US of A (as much as they'd like to claim it). Additionally, other pantheons outside of the West have their own timelines that explain how historical events interacted with mythological ones, but I don't pretend to be well-versed enough to explain those histories.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24666-ravian","name":"Ravian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-24T14:09:43-07:00","id":1420018,"title":"","content":"I will mention the more recent example of Francois Duvalier, the President (read brutally repressive dictator) of Haiti from 1957 to 1971. He heavily pushed Haitian Vodou as part of a nationalist-populist agenda, eventually claiming to be a Vodou priest and deliberately modeling his public image after that of the Baron Samedi, while also claiming to be the physical embodiment of the nation (and the personally chosen of Jesus Christ). <br /> <br /> An extra layer of theological weirdness in all of this is that the only foreign head of state to visit Haiti during Duvalier's rule was Emperor Haile Selassie of Ethiopia, the man considered the second coming of Jesus and/or the Messiah by a sizable segment of the Rastafarian faith. <br /> <br /> (Also, the even worse dictator of Equatorial Guinea, Macias Nguema, who actually changed the nation's motto to &quot;There is no other god but Macias Ngeuma.&quot;)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-24T15:41:44-07:00","id":1420033,"title":"","content":"By the way. Why couldn't the American national motto remain &quot;E Pluribus Unum&quot; (Out of many One)?<br /> <br /> More importantly, although it is fashionable to sneer at the USA and say we are worthless and have done nothing of worth, we really are important in world history for making a Republic, and what was for the time a shockingly democratic one, and making it last. Few republics lasted long, and fewer stayed anything like democratic for long, and most that lasted were tiny. It would have a Mythic shadow. I know all the Gatekeepers that own this site will attack me, but we are that important.<br /> <br /> And on the Mythic front. Several myths proclaimed that Ben Franklin got the idea for how to set up the government from the Iroquois Confederation. That's totally wrong. Franklin thought our government wasn't nearly democratic enough (and he was right) and besides Hamilton got most of the ideas by stealing then from the Brits. But that to the side, both Native Americans and Euro-Americans proclaimed a Native American mythic origin for American democracy. <br /> <br /> That means the various Native American pantheons can claim for any of dozens of reasons that they made America a democracy. And they could point to the CSA, the robber barons of the &quot;gilded age&quot;, the KKK, the House Unamerican Activities Committee, Richard Nixon, et al, to say it wasn't easy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 10-24-2020, 07:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-24T16:46:18-07:00","id":1420043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1419123-why-don-t-scions-conquer-the-world?p=1420033#post1420033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way. Why couldn't the American national motto remain &quot;E Pluribus Unum&quot; (Out of many One)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Given how recently the change to One Nation Under God was made, that seems quite reasonable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> More importantly, although it is fashionable to sneer at the USA and say we are worthless and have done nothing of worth, we really are important in world history for making a Republic, and what was for the time a shockingly democratic one, and making it last. Few republics lasted long, and fewer stayed anything like democratic for long, and most that lasted were tiny. It would have a Mythic shadow. I know all the Gatekeepers that own this site will attack me, but we are that important. </div> </div> </div>I don't think many people would dismiss the United States as being without influence. They might suggest that the nature of that influence is something that can't be reduced to positive and negative entries in an accounts book, but I doubt there's anyone on these forums who would say, &quot;America? What have they ever done?&quot; I could be wrong, though; I'm not a Gatekeeper.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And on the Mythic front. Several myths proclaimed that Ben Franklin got the idea for how to set up the government from the Iroquois Confederation. That's totally wrong. Franklin thought our government wasn't nearly democratic enough (and he was right) and besides Hamilton got most of the ideas by stealing then from the Brits. But that to the side, both Native Americans and Euro-Americans proclaimed a Native American mythic origin for American democracy. </div> </div> </div>This is interesting (because I am also neither American nor a historian), but I wonder how far it stretches the definition of &quot;myth&quot; toward &quot;common perception.&quot; My curiosity doesn't have much to do with the overall purpose of this thread, though, so it's not something you need to feel the need to address.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That means the various Native American pantheons can claim for any of dozens of reasons that they made America a democracy. And they could point to the CSA, the robber barons of the &quot;gilded age&quot;, the KKK, the House Unamerican Activities Committee, Richard Nixon, et al, to say it wasn't easy. </div> </div> </div>A few pantheons might be able to make that claim, although if I were writing them, I'd want to look more carefully at how the cultures to which those pantheons are connected have incorporated (if they have) colonial contact into their own religious traditions. I'm sure there are some examples out there, and there are certainly post-contact examples of religious innovation on the part of indigenous populations. I just don't know how widespread they are.<br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> Back on the main topic, although still loosely connected to this post, one bit of advice I'd give for people who want to include stories about World-conquering Scions is to think about them from a player perspective as well as an in-game one. If someone has lived their life in the shadow of colonialism, they might not find the idea of imposing that on someone else quite as fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Scion 2E</b> Freelancer: <i>Origin; Hero; Demigod; God; Mythical Denizens; Mysteries of the World; Saints &amp; Monsters; No Gods, No Masters; Once &amp; Future, Realms of Magic &amp; Mystery</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/369-geoffrey","name":"Geoffrey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-25T00:30:33-07:00","id":1420088,"title":"","content":"So a few thoughts strike me as optional. Of course there's conquest through other means, ie run a fortune 500 and that sort of thing. However, a few things come to mind, consider how the world is these days, how often do you think conquest oriented Scions end up satisfying their conquest ambitions without needing to go large scale? I mean consider the fiction we get in the God book deals with a Scion who ascends to full divinity in their pantheon, to be guardian of a city.<br /> <br /> So what about incidents where its less conquer the world and more become the de facto power on earth for the state, or the city, or whatever their area of interest is?<br /> <br /> Granted I also had an idea of a Scion that really wants to do the world conqueror routine, but keeps getting waylaid by the fact that they're tied into a specific mythology and crap just keeps coming up that stops the world conquest from happening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-25T08:55:55-07:00","id":1420130,"title":"","content":"one word, fatebinding. <br /> <br /> at least that's the reason why they haven't conquered the world in the first edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-25T10:43:30-07:00","id":1420146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1419123-why-don-t-scions-conquer-the-world?p=1420033#post1420033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> More importantly, although it is fashionable to sneer at the USA and say we are worthless and have done nothing of worth, we really are important in world history for making a Republic, and what was for the time a shockingly democratic one, and making it last. Few republics lasted long, and fewer stayed anything like democratic for long, and most that lasted were tiny. It would have a Mythic shadow. I know all the Gatekeepers that own this site will attack me, but we are that important.</div> </div> </div> </div>the argument you are referring to was about excluding the bad stuff (especially With a goddess who was a propaganda symbol for Manifest Destiny), no one was arguing for erasing the positive - just that the negative needed full examination and inclusion too. The only thing that\u2019s going to get you attacked is grossly misrepresenting other people\u2019s point entirely.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-25T13:34:35-07:00","id":1420168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1419123-why-don-t-scions-conquer-the-world?p=1420033#post1420033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way. Why couldn't the American national motto remain &quot;E Pluribus Unum&quot; (Out of many One)?<br /> <br /> More importantly, although it is fashionable to sneer at the USA and say we are worthless and have done nothing of worth, we really are important in world history for making a Republic</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is neither the forum nor the topic for starting a nationalistic rant. Leave the thread please.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-25T15:09:49-07:00","id":1420172,"title":"","content":"But yes, I think this is one of those statements that the book keeps vague for the purpose of &quot;Flavor to Personal Taste&quot;. If the idea of nations of the World now being more theocratic by virtue of the Gods directly blessing the leaders, you can reduce it. If your players want to become Heads of States, then go for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favo